   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is a white woman in her mid-twenties with dark brown, wavy, shoulder-length hair, whose movement comes from <Video 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] <Subject 1> does jumping jacks on a sandy beach at sunset.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the woman's hairstyle and outfit are retained.\n<Video 1> (motion source): attribute_transfer - the movement of the person in <Video 1> is transferred to <Subject 1>; that person's appearance and surroundings do not appear.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, full-color cinematic shot in warm, low sunset light.\n[Shot 1] A full-body shot, framed from head to toe, shows <Subject 1>, the young woman with dark brown wavy hair, wearing a red t-shirt, black leggings and white sneakers, standing on a wide sandy beach at sunset with gentle waves rolling in behind her. She does jumping jacks in a steady rhythm: she jumps her feet apart while swinging her straight arms up over her head, then jumps her feet back together as her arms come down to her sides, again and again. She moves exactly as the person in <Video 1> does, with the same rhythm and timing. The camera holds steady at waist height and keeps her whole body in frame.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nGentle waves and a light sea breeze; no voices.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
    352,
    608,
    124,
    "match"
   ],
   "title": "Test shot (<Video 1> = the clip)"
