    "## 11. Video to RefCap\nStores **one clip** in a RefCap: its video latent and the 2 fps frames the text encoder reads, as clip 1 of `models/refcaps/<name>.safetensors`. A test shot renders it as `<Video 1>` at the end. One queue runs it all.\n\n**Steps**\n1. Load the clip in **Your clip**. H3 reads reference frames as **24 fps**, so a 30 fps clip plays 20% slower; **Frame rate** shows what you loaded. Convert others first: `ffmpeg -i in.mp4 -vf fps=24 out.mp4`. Keep it at 720p or below, because every frame is decoded at full size before the scale (about 4 GB of RAM for 5 s of 1080p).\n2. Set the **Trim**. H3 cuts a reference clip to the length you render at, and the build node's `orbit_length` (124 frames, 5.2 s) must equal it; the trim picks where that window starts. The model card asks for 2-15 s per clip, 15 s in total and at most 3 clips per shot.\n3. **Scale** sets the cost. At 608 px a 124-frame clip costs 7,733 reference tokens on every step, as much as the 608x352 render itself; at 720p it would be 32,560. At 304 px it is about a quarter.\n4. Set `name` and `description` on the build node and queue. Refresh the browser so the file appears in the RefCap lists.\n\n**Using it**\n- A movement for a character: workflow 12. To edit a finished clip: workflow 14. For a place, stills from the walk do better than the clip (workflow 15), and a camera move is best said in words (workflow 13). In any pack (workflow 7), *Select* the RefCap with `views` = `none` and `clips` = `1`, after the character's RefCap. Pictures are numbered first, then clips as `<Video 1..3>`.\n- Name what the clip is for in the prompt, as MiniMax's guide does: a movement (`<Subject 1> is the woman whose appearance comes from <Picture 1> and whose movement comes from <Video 1>.`), or only the camera's path (`[reference generation]`, `<Video 1> (camera movement): weak_reference - ...`).\n- The test is fed the scaled frames directly, which matches replaying the saved RefCap bit for bit. Mute the *Test render* group (select it, Ctrl+M) to skip the test.\n\n**Settings in these workflows** follow ComfyUI's MiniMax H3 reference-to-video template: the ref2va model with its 4-step Lightning LoRA, 4 steps, `res_multistep` + `simple`, 608x352. For the base model, bypass the *Lightning LoRA* node and use 20 steps. The measurements quoted here ran on a community H3 turbo finetune (shift 6/3, 8 steps) on a 12 GB GPU. Raise the size and length for final renders; the reference tokens ride through every step, so more photos and larger captures cost time."
   ],
